    'ecosystem' => 'StageWatch is the time in the Patterns ecosystem, and it hears Patterns, AGMessage and PlayMap on the venue network by itself. Linked Patterns stage pages follow its clock, its VT countdown follows the clip on air in Patterns or PlayMap, AGMessage shows the live stage timer to the whole meeting and puts the research team\'s answers on the confidence monitor, and PlayMap can map the timer onto any surface. StageWatch is also the approval desk, where one person approves the AI suggestions from Patterns, AGMessage and connected AI agents.',
    'architecture' => [
        ['title' => 'One clock, every screen', 'text' => 'Every screen counts from the same show clock and corrects itself on every update, so screens stay in step and a device\'s own clock never matters.'],
        ['title' => 'The show comes first', 'text' => 'A slow phone, a busy network or a stalled device can never hold up the show clock or the desk.'],
        ['title' => 'Local by design', 'text' => 'StageWatch runs on the venue\'s own network with no cloud service, account or licence server, so the show keeps going when the internet doesn\'t.'],
        ['title' => 'Back on its feet', 'text' => 'A watchdog brings StageWatch straight back after a crash with the show where it was, saves can\'t be torn, and a power cut costs a restart, not the show.'],
        ['title' => 'Screens that tell the truth', 'text' => 'A screen that loses contact says NOT CONNECTED rather than showing a confident wrong time, and commands from keys, remotes and other apps get a receipt that says whether they were done or refused, and why.'],
        ['title' => 'One way in', 'text' => 'Buttons, Stream Deck keys, browser remotes, other apps and AI agents all drive StageWatch through the same commands, so none of them can do anything an operator can\'t.'],
    ],
